Authorship
  The Atkinson Hyperlegible typeface was created by the Braille Institute of
  America, Inc. and is named after its founder, J. Robert Atkinson. The Next
  and Mono families extend that work; their own copyright notices read
  "The Atkinson Hyperlegible Next Project Authors" and "The Atkinson
  Hyperlegible Mono Project Authors", and they are developed in the
  googlefonts organisation on GitHub:

    https://github.com/googlefonts/atkinson-hyperlegible-next
    https://github.com/googlefonts/atkinson-hyperlegible-next-mono

  Development home is not the same as authorship or as a runtime dependency:
  this package serves the files from the consuming project's own origin and
  contacts no font host.

Modification
  The shipped files are subsets, produced by tools/subset-fonts.mjs from
  @fontsource-variable/atkinson-hyperlegible-next 5.3.0 and
  @fontsource-variable/atkinson-hyperlegible-mono 5.3.0. Glyphs outside the
  documented Latin ranges were removed; no outline, metric or axis was
  altered, and the weight axis still spans 200 to 800.

  The upstream copyright notice declares no Reserved Font Name, so the subsets
  keep the original family names, as the licence permits.
